{
 "_what": "Coordinates for the board's location nodes, keyed by node id: latitude, longitude, the place as written (\"Roswell, New Mexico, USA\"), and which of `_sources` they came from. Read by tools/regrade.py, which folds them onto the location entities as `coords` and `locLabel`, and by tools/build_places.py, which ships app/public/data/places.json for the #/places page.",
 "_why": "Redesign phase 11 moved the 76-entry table that had been written into tools/regrade.py out of the code and into research/, where a coordinate is data with a stated source rather than a constant in a script. The values were moved verbatim; none was added or changed, and one (l-ames, under `_withheld`) was set aside because it contradicts its node. Some keys are ids the board no longer carries (merged or renamed nodes); they are kept so the move changes nothing, and they place nothing.",
